<exercise>
	<title>The collection of all unit vectors</title>

	<task>

		<statement><p>
			Suppose every possible unit vector in <m> \R^2 </m> was placed with initial point at the origin.
			What shape would the collection of all terminal points of these vectors trace out?
		</p></statement>

		<answer><p> The unit circle, centred at the origin. </p></answer>

	</task>

	<task>

		<statement><p>
			Suppose every possible vector of the form <m> \uvec{x} = 5 \uvec{u} </m> in <m> \R^2 </m>,
			where <m> \uvec{u} </m> is a unit vector,
			was placed with initial point at the origin.
			What shape would the collection of all terminal points of these vectors trace out?
		</p></statement>

		<answer><p> A circle of radius <m> 5 </m>, centred at the origin. </p></answer>

	</task>

	<task>

		<statement><p>
			Suppose every possible unit vector in <m> \R^3 </m> was placed with initial point at the origin.
			What shape would the collection of all terminal points of these vectors trace out?
		</p></statement>

		<answer><p> The unit sphere, centred at the origin. </p></answer>

	</task>

</exercise>

